## What changed, briefly

1. Renamed the existing `DS4_REASONING_EFFORT_MAX_PREFIX` → `_HIGH_PREFIX` (same text, correct tier) and added the real `_MAX_PREFIX` with the official "max" text.
2. `chat_push_think_prefix()` (ds4.c) and `render_deepseek_chat_prompt_text()` (ds4_server.c) — the two independent prompt-rendering paths that both had this bug — now branch on `DS4_THINK_HIGH` as well as `DS4_THINK_MAX`, not just the latter.
3. `ds4_think_mode_for_context()` is now a documented no-op rather than removed outright, since four `ds4_server.c` call sites use it and `ds4_think_max_min_context()` may still be useful to advise clients on the (correct) output-length guideline.
4. Added `test_render_think_high_prompt_prefix()` (there was previously zero test coverage for the "high" tier ever rendering anything), fixed the now-incorrect context-gate assertion in `test_reasoning_effort_mapping()`, and added a mutual-exclusivity assertion to the existing max-tier test.

## Testing

`make ds4_test` passes clean (`ds4 tests: ok`, zero failures) against the full existing suite plus the new/updated assertions. Also smoke-tested live against a real 0731 quant — `reasoning_effort: high` and `: max` now produce visibly distinct prompts, `: max` no longer collapses to the "high" text at contexts below 384K.

Happy to open this as a PR if useful rather than leaving it as a comment — let me know which you'd prefer.

