Running this PR (both commits, including the DS4_THINK_LOW tier from the follow-up) rebased onto current `main` (`84cc882`) on M3 Ultra Metal surfaced two small compatibility gaps with code that landed upstream after this branch was opened. Sharing the fixup that made the rebase clean, in case it saves a round-trip when this gets refreshed:

1. **`ds4_cli.c`: `repl_glm_reasoning_effort_text()`** — upstream added this switch over `ds4_think_mode`; with the new `DS4_THINK_LOW` enum value it no longer compiles (unhandled case). LOW behaves like the DeepSeek default: thinking enabled, no effort prefix, so it returns NULL like NONE.
2. **`ds4_server.c`: `render_glm_chat_prompt_text()`** — the GLM render does `effort ? effort : "Reasoning Effort: Max"`, so a LOW request (which intentionally has no prefix text) silently renders as **Max** — the exact "low means the biggest prompt" failure mode this PR fixes for DeepSeek, resurfacing on the GLM path. Guarding the `<|system|>` block on `effort != NULL` fixes it.

```diff
--- a/ds4_cli.c
+++ b/ds4_cli.c
@@ -1333,6 +1333,7 @@ static const char *repl_glm_reasoning_effort_text(ds4_think_mode mode) {
     switch (mode) {
     case DS4_THINK_HIGH: return "Reasoning Effort: High";
     case DS4_THINK_MAX:  return "Reasoning Effort: Max";
+    case DS4_THINK_LOW:  return NULL;
     case DS4_THINK_NONE: return NULL;
     }
     return NULL;
--- a/ds4_server.c
+++ b/ds4_server.c
@@ -2559,8 +2559,10 @@ static char *render_glm_chat_prompt_text(const chat_msgs *msgs,
     buf_puts(&out, "[gMASK]<sop>");
     if (think) {
         const char *effort = ds4_glm_reasoning_effort_text(think_mode);
-        buf_puts(&out, "<|system|>");
-        buf_puts(&out, effort ? effort : "Reasoning Effort: Max");
+        if (effort) {
+            buf_puts(&out, "<|system|>");
+            buf_puts(&out, effort);
+        }
     }
```

Plus a server-side regression test mirroring the existing prefix tests: a LOW render must contain no `Reasoning Effort:` text while still ending thinking-enabled (`<|assistant|><think>`), so it can't silently fall back to the GLM Max default again.

With that fixup: warning-free build, full `make test` green on M3 Ultra Metal, and the PR's own reasoning-effort mapping tests pass unchanged. Happy to push the fixup somewhere if useful.

